# Thinking

Thinking is framed as a universal mental model—a conceptual tool for navigating complex situations through pattern and relationship recognition. It provides mental shortcuts and frameworks for making sense of complexity across all domains.

This source cross-references five key works:
- [[Six Thinking Hats - Edward de Bono]]
- [[Lateral Thinking_ Creativity Step by Step - Edward de Bono]]
- [[How to Decide - Annie Duke]]
- [[Clear Thinking_ Turning Ordinary Moments into Extraordinary Results - Shane Parrish]]
- [[The Great Mental Models Vol 1 - Shane Parrish]]

Confidence: 0.7
Applicability: Universal
